  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Speaking and writing",
     "texto": [
      "In everyday conversation the **Perfekt** is used: **Ich habe gestern gearbeitet** (yesterday I worked). In written texts, stories and news the **Präteritum** is used: **Gestern arbeitete ich lange** (yesterday I worked for a long time).",
      "With **sein**, **haben** and the modal verbs, the Präteritum is also used in conversation: **Ich hatte keine Zeit** (I didn't have time)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When, in the past",
     "texto": [
      "**Als** means \"when\" in the past and is used once: **Als ich klein war, wohnte ich in Madrid** (when I was little I lived in Madrid). The verb in the sentence with «als» goes to the end.",
      "Don't confuse it with **wenn** (when, if, in the present or future)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Ordering the story",
     "texto": [
      "**Zuerst** (first), **dann** (then), **danach** (after that) and **schließlich** (finally) mark the order of events.",
      "Example: **Zuerst ging ich in die Schule, dann kam ich nach Hause.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
